  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be maintained in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation and Block Plan - E00\rProposed Location and Block Plan - P00\rProposed Ground and First Floor Plan - P01\rProposed Loft and Roof Plan - P02\rProposed Front and Left-Side Elevation Plan - P03\rProposed Rear and Right-Side Elevation Plan - P04\rProposed Section AA Plan - P05\rProposed Cycle Storage Plan - P06\rHighways proforma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining rooms shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area\r",
    "Prior to occupation, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, together with details of bin collection access in accordance with the Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support \rof the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The glazing serving second floor outrigger dormer flank window of the development indicated on drawing No P03 shall be in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 3 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority.\r \rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015, or any amending Order, no balustrades or other means of enclosure shall be erected on the roof of the extension(s). No roof of any part of the extension(s) shall be used for any recreational purpose and access shall only be for the purposes of the maintenance of the property or means of emergency escape. \r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining properties.\r"
  ],
